4 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 5 0 R
  /Title (1.1 On your last todo list project, the application was developed with a really basic architecture; An html web page, a web API, and some TypeScript functions to handle app interactivity. Nowadays, using vanilla JavaScript or TypeScript to create web applications is not a common practice (eventually for small applications). Most of the time, web frameworks or libraries are used to create web applications. They provide a structure to your codebase, simplifies some tasks and provide reusability of code.)
  /Dest 311 0 R
>>
endobj

5 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 6 0 R
  /Prev 4 0 R
  /Title (1.2 There are many popular web frameworks, such as Angular, Vue, Svelte or Solid. In 2026, the most popular one is React. React is a library created by Facebook in 2013. Used by many big companies such as Facebook, Instagram, Netflix, Airbnb and smaller ones. React is based on components, which are reusable pieces of code that represent a part of the user interface (like functions but for UI). Components can be nested, managed and handled independently, which allows for complex applications to be built from simple building blocks.)
  /Dest 312 0 R
>>
endobj

6 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Next 7 0 R
  /Prev 5 0 R
  /Title (1.3 As for programming languages, there is no "best" framework, each one has its own advantages and disadvantages. But React is a good choice for this project because it is widely used, has a large community and a lot of resources available online. Moreover, React is often used with TypeScript, which you already know. This will offer you a good starting point with web frameworks.)
  /Dest 313 0 R
>>
endobj

7 0 obj
<<
  /Parent 3 0 R
  /Prev 6 0 R
  /Title (1.4 The goal of this project is to help you understand and apply modern front-end development practices by rebuilding your existing to-do list application using React. Through this exercise, you will learn how to structure a React application, interact with a RESTful API, and implement reusable components.)
  /Dest 314 0 R
>>
endobj

